---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What Agent Skills are and how to install them from skills.merze.ai into ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, or Claude Code."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <article class="prose about-page">
    <h1>About Agent Skills</h1>
    <p>
      Agent Skills are folders of instructions that agents can load on demand.
      Each skill is a directory with a <code>SKILL.md</code> file (YAML
      frontmatter + markdown body) and optional supporting files. Use them in
      public ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, Claude Code, and other skill-capable
      agents.
    </p>

    <h2>Install a skill</h2>
    <p>
      Open any skill in the catalog. Copy the install command, or download every
      listed file and place them under <code>&lt;slug&gt;/</code> in your
      agent’s skills directory, then reload so the agent discovers the skill.
      Skill pages also offer a chat-agent paste with links to
      <code>SKILL.md</code> and supporting files for ChatGPT-style agents.
    </p>
    <p>
      Typical install from this catalog:
    </p>
    <pre><code>npx skills add https://skills.merze.ai --skill &lt;name&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2>Skill layout</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Folder at the catalog root named with the skill slug (lowercase
        letters, digits, and hyphens; max 64 characters).
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>SKILL.md</code> with required frontmatter:
        <ul>
          <li><code>name</code> — must match the folder name</li>
          <li><code>description</code> — 1–1024 characters</li>
          <li>
            Optional <code>metadata.version</code>, <code>source</code>,
            <code>category</code>, <code>tags</code>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
        Optional supporting markdown (and allowlisted text/data files) published
        beside <code>SKILL.md</code>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This site rebuilds from every root <code>*/SKILL.md</code>. Invalid
      <code>name</code> or <code>description</code>, a name/folder mismatch, or
      a disallowed file type in a skill folder fails the build.
    </p>

    <h2>Merze</h2>
    <p>
      Skills are published by
      <a href="https://merze.ai">Merze</a>. For contributions or questions,
      contact Merze through <a href="https://merze.ai">merze.ai</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
